<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The LaunchAgent `SMAppService` registers, sealed into Janela.app at build time.

  MUST NOT be written, rewritten or generated at runtime. `smd` runs a static code
  signature check on the whole bundle before it will load this file, so a plist added
  or edited after signing breaks the seal and registration fails with
  errSecCSBadResource (-67054) on every signed install — the exact failure that shows
  up on a user's machine and never in CI. `scripts/verify-bundle.ts` asserts the file
  is listed in the bundle's sealed resources.

  No `Sockets` key, and so no socket activation: the daemon binds
  `~/.janela/run/janelad.sock` itself in a 0700 directory it owns
  (`packages/daemon/src/endpoint.ts`). A launchd-created socket would publish its path
  only into the GUI login session's launchd environment, which a CLI over ssh cannot
  read, and would tie the address to launchd — both of which a portable client rules
  out. Socket activation was given up in #39, 2026-09-08.

  No `RunAtLoad` either: registering must not start a daemon nobody asked for. A
  client that fails to connect starts it with
  `launchctl kickstart gui/<uid>/sh.janela.janelad` and retries.

  No `StandardOutPath` / `StandardErrorPath` either. launchd takes a literal path with
  no `~` expansion, and this file is sealed once for every user of the machine, so the
  only path it could name is a shared one — which is also a symlink trap — and it would
  do nothing for a daemon a developer runs in the foreground. The daemon writes its own
  log to `~/Library/Logs/sh.janela.Janela/janelad.log` (`apps/daemon/src/log-file.ts`),
  the same place in both modes, and mirrors it to stderr in the foreground. #45.
  (An XML comment may not contain two hyphens in a row, which is why the flag is not
  spelled here.)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>sh.janela.janelad</string>
  <!-- Relative to the bundle root, which only SMAppService-installed agents may use.
       Tauri's bundler puts sidecars in Contents/MacOS, not Contents/Resources. -->
  <key>BundleProgram</key>
  <string>Contents/MacOS/janelad</string>
  <!-- Crash -> launchd restarts it. Deliberate exit (idle, or the user stopping the
       background service) -> it stays down. -->
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <dict>
    <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
    <false/>
  </dict>
  <!-- The daemon hosts the user's builds and agents. launchd's default for an agent
       is Background, which I/O- and CPU-throttles everything underneath it. -->
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Interactive</string>
</dict>
</plist>
